      "value": "This idea lack a severe volume of looking into the future and consiquences of that kind of system. I think it's easier if i break it into a few key Points:\n1. First of all - what issue is that trying to prevent? \"Not only would malicious users not see your main avatar upon initialization\" - I think you mean this is suppose to prevent stealing of avatar? Sure, it will work in a short perspective, and your avatars will get some kind of safety, but, and only BUT from people not from your friends list, and the point where i'm going - what if your avatars will be stolen even after implimentaion? What are you gonna do THEN, delete hundreds of friends? And what if even that wont work, will you add those deleted friends back after finding out traitor? People, especially creators, will become extremely suspicious of whom they friend, i can't imagine how much of an anxiety that will give to them, to decide if it's safe to add a person or not, is he just pretending/pretended to be nice, but in reality - just want to steal my stuff?\n2. Second point comes directly from first: if everybody(or most of the people) will have this feature on - what then? try to remember times when YOU guys started to play, were everyone Brushes and standart avatars? are YOU gonna add more friends, just from how they talk, without seeing their avatar at all? are YOU gonna be happy, to come to a friend and see 10 standart avatars, and only 2 of your friends? This will destroy the whole point of vrchat - meeting people, and connecting to them, when everybody have a special personality - their avatars. You said the feture should be by deafulte off, but you just place people in a position where they can either \"be safe\" and their avatar won't be stolen, or they can risk and meet new people, ask yourself - what will you choose, and how many NEW friends (especially considering first point and suspicious, or anxiety of avatar safety) will you add in a future with that system?(and yes, i assume that MOST of people are not using custom fallbacks, since creaton of such takes tons of effort, and avatar creators will not provide them with main avatar, at least not without additional payment)\n3. What about perfomance result of that? how much of a personal, server and internet speed perfomance will that take? additional checks  and requests, potential to abuse, since, if you switch that constantly - people on others side they will have to load you fallback, then normal avatar, and then back in a circles few times a second, how to prevent that?\nAnd surely some stuff i forgot, but in general - System like that has a potential to destroy current social system, break already established connections between people and ruin ways to make new friends, without providing any replacement, ask yourself - is it really worth, especially considering it's not even giving you a 100% safety from a problem you're trying to solve in a first place?\nP.S. I'm sure that avatar and assets stealing is a problem that has to be solved, especially considering incoming economy system, but that surely not the way for it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
