  "details": "I was discussing with a friend regarding people hotswapping/ripping avatars and they thought of an idea that could help mitigate future spread of this issue, revitalize publics and MAYBE put an end to the future of ripperstore (an asset redistributing website filled with stolen avatars).\nThink of this, let's say there was a fallback system like what we currently have but for nonfriends or non whitelisted users. People would have their main avatars viewable to specifically friends and whitelisted users whilst others would see a chosen avatar we selected? Not only would malicious users not see your main avatar upon initialization but would also allow users to selectively choose who they want to view it. Furthermore, it could allow people to join their friends in publics without the whole switching to a disposable model every time and the hassle behind it. It would also prevent friends of friends of friends from joining and just yoinking your avatar, Friends+ would no longer just be a a discount public lobby/random gateway for people to join and could be safe aswell. I've had my avatars stolen countless of times without even stepping a foot in public. I'm seeing this from a avatar creator perspective and I hope other creators would agree with me. Asset stealing is a HUGE issue in VRChat and we definitely need a way to atleast mitigate or slow down the process behind this. I've known multiple people around the community who's gotten their days/months work stolen from in a blink of an eye and reuploaded publicly. This feature could also alleviate stress on the support team, all of the previous features are already implemented (Fallback avatars, safety, whitelist/blacklist) but I think this could be a valid security feature on top of that. And with the announcement of the VRC avatar economy I think this should be a priority and there is absolutely no doubt in my mind a NEED for avatar security before anything gets implemented. \n***This feature could be disabled by default to prevent new users who arent familiar with the system to not question why other users don't see their avatars.***\nI would love to hear what the community thinks of the idea.\nThank you",
